# Testing

How the tests of <%= @module %> are run and written. What a test is for in a given area is in that
area's `AGENTS.md`.

## Running

| | Command |
| --- | --- |
| One file, during TDD | `mix test test/<%= @app %>_web/health_test.exs:12` |
| The suite | `mix test` |
| The gate, before every commit | `mix precommit` |
| The docs alone | `mix test test/harness_test.exs` |

The suite needs a running PostgreSQL, configured in `config/test.exs`. CI checks the project with
`ehosctl verify`, with only the test environment's dependencies (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`); run
it yourself to check exactly what CI checks.

## The loop

Red, green, refactor. Write the failing test first and watch it fail for the reason you expect.
Write the minimum that passes, then clean up with the test green. Run only the file you are
working on while you iterate, and `mix precommit` once before the PR.

## A contract's command

Test a command the way a caller reaches it: through `/api`, with a credential.
`EhOsContract.Auth.Testing` gives a test a key the application trusts (`pin_keys: true` in
`config/test.exs`) and `credential/2`, which issues a credential with the capabilities named.
<%= if @example do %>`test/<%= @app %>_web/entries_api_test.exs` is the pattern:<% else %>The pattern:<% end %>

- one test with a credential that holds the command's capability, which expects it to succeed;
- `assert_every_entry_refuses/2` over the contracts, which checks that every command refuses a
  credential without its capability;
- one call without a credential, refused with 401.

Every append to the engine's log takes one lock, held for the sandbox's whole transaction, so a
test that dispatches is `async: false`. Every invariant also has a `rejected` scenario in its
contract, which `EhOsContract.ScenarioCase` turns into a test of the implementation.

`config/test.exs` sets `subscriptions: :manual`: reactions delivered at least once do not run on
their own in tests, so a test that needs one runs it explicitly.

## Tests the template wrote

- `test/<%= @app %>_web/health_test.exs`: the health endpoints, live always and ready once the
  application holds a key.
- `test/harness_test.exs`: the docs. Relative links and `docs/*.md` paths resolve; `AGENTS.md`,
  `README.md`, `VISION.md` and every `SKILL.md` stay within 200 lines, `ARCHITECTURE.md` and
  `docs/*.md` within 400, `TESTING.md` within 300; nothing cites an ADR; every skill in
  `.agents/skills/` is linked from `.claude/skills/`.

## Rules

- **A test must fail when the thing it guards is removed.** Undo the fix, run the test, and see
  red before you push.
- **No network, no wall clock, no shared state between tests** unless the test is about them. An
  `async` test never changes `Application` env.
